2371: <h3 id=node-trees>Node tree</h3>
2372: 
2373: <p><dfn export id=concept-node>Nodes</dfn> are objects that <a>implement</a> {{Node}}.
2374: <a for=/>Nodes</a> <a>participate</a> in a <a>tree</a>, which is known as the
2375: <dfn export id=concept-node-tree>node tree</dfn>.
2376: 
2377: <div class=note>
2378:  <p>In practice you deal with more specific objects.
2379: 
2380:  <p>Objects that <a>implement</a> {{Node}} also implement an inherited interface: {{Document}},
2381:  {{DocumentType}}, {{DocumentFragment}}, {{Element}}, {{CharacterData}}, or {{Attr}}.
2382: 
2383:  <p>Objects that implement {{DocumentFragment}} sometimes implement {{ShadowRoot}}.
2384: 
2385:  <p>Objects that implement {{Element}} also typically implement an inherited interface, such as
2386:  {{HTMLAnchorElement}}.
2387: 
2388:  <p>Objects that implement {{CharacterData}} also implement an inherited interface: {{Text}},
2389:  {{ProcessingInstruction}}, or {{Comment}}.
2390: 
2391:  <p>Objects that implement {{Text}} sometimes implement {{CDATASection}}.
2392: 
2393:  <p>Thus, every [=/node=]'s [=primary interface=] is one of: {{Document}}, {{DocumentType}},
2394:  {{DocumentFragment}}, {{ShadowRoot}}, {{Element}} or an inherited interface of {{Element}},
2395:  {{Attr}}, {{Text}}, {{CDATASection}}, {{ProcessingInstruction}}, or {{Comment}}.
2396: </div>
2397: 
2398: <p>For brevity, this specification refers to an object that <a>implements</a> {{Node}} and an
2399: inherited interface <code><var>NodeInterface</var></code>, as a
2400: <code><var>NodeInterface</var></code> <a for=/>node</a>.
2401: 
2402: <p>A <a>node tree</a> is constrained as follows, expressed as a relationship between a
2403: <a for=/>node</a> and its potential <a for=tree>children</a>:
2404: 
2405: <dl>
2406:  <dt>{{Document}}
2407:  <dd>
2408:   <p>In <a>tree order</a>:
2409:   <ol>
2410:    <li><p>Zero or more {{ProcessingInstruction}} or {{Comment}} <a for=/>nodes</a>.
2411:    <li><p>Optionally one {{DocumentType}} <a for=/>node</a>.
2412:    <li><p>Zero or more {{ProcessingInstruction}} or {{Comment}} <a for=/>nodes</a>.
2413:    <li><p>Optionally one {{Element}} <a for=/>node</a>.
2414:    <li><p>Zero or more {{ProcessingInstruction}} or {{Comment}} <a for=/>nodes</a>.
2415:   </ol>
2416: 
2417:  <dt>{{DocumentFragment}}
2418:  <dt>{{Element}}
2419:  <dd><p>Zero or more {{Element}} or {{CharacterData}} <a for=/>nodes</a>.
2420: 
2421:  <dt>{{DocumentType}}
2422:  <dt>{{CharacterData}}
2423:  <dt>{{Attr}}
2424:  <dd><p>No <a for=tree>children</a>.
2425: </dl>
2426: 
2427: <p class=note>{{Attr}} <a for=/>nodes</a> <a>participate</a> in a <a>tree</a> for historical
2428: reasons; they never have a (non-null) <a for=tree>parent</a> or any <a for=tree>children</a> and are
2429: therefore alone in a <a>tree</a>.
2430: 
2431: <p>To determine the <dfn export id=concept-node-length for=Node>length</dfn> of a <a for=/>node</a>
2432: <var>node</var>, run these steps:
2433: 
2434: <ol>
2435:  <li><p>If <var>node</var> is a {{DocumentType}} or {{Attr}} <a for=/>node</a>, then return 0.
2436: 
2437:  <li><p>If <var>node</var> is a {{CharacterData}} <a for=/>node</a>, then return <var>node</var>'s
2438:  <a for=CharacterData>data</a>'s <a for=string>length</a>.
2439: 
2440:  <li><p>Return the number of <var>node</var>'s <a for=tree>children</a>.
2441: </ol>
2442: 
2443: <p>A <a for=/>node</a> is considered <dfn export id=concept-node-empty for=Node>empty</dfn> if its
2444: <a for=Node>length</a> is 0.
2445: 
2446: 
2447: <h4 id=document-trees>Document tree</h4>
2448: 
2449: <p>A <dfn export id=concept-document-tree>document tree</dfn> is a <a>node tree</a> whose
2450: <a for=tree>root</a> is a <a for=/>document</a>.
2451: 
2452: <p>The <dfn export>document element</dfn> of a <a for=/>document</a> is the <a for=/>element</a>
2453: whose <a for=tree>parent</a> is that <a for=/>document</a>, if it exists; otherwise null.
2454: 
2455: <p class=note>Per the <a>node tree</a> constraints, there can be only one such
2456: <a for=/>element</a>.
2457: 
2458: <p>A <a for=/>node</a> is <dfn export>in a document tree</dfn> if its <a for=tree>root</a> is a
2459: <a for=/>document</a>.
2460: 
2461: <p>A <a for=/>node</a> is <dfn export>in a document</dfn> if it is <a>in a document tree</a>.
2462: <span class=note>The term <a>in a document</a> is no longer supposed to be used. It indicates that
2463: the standard using it has not been updated to account for <a>shadow trees</a>.</span>
2464: 
2465: 
2466: <h4 id=shadow-trees>Shadow tree</h4>
2467: 
2468: <p>A <dfn export id=concept-shadow-tree>shadow tree</dfn> is a <a>node tree</a> whose
2469: <a for=tree>root</a> is a <a for=/>shadow root</a>.
2470: 
2471: <p>A <a for=/>shadow root</a> is always attached to another <a>node tree</a> through its
2472: <a for=DocumentFragment>host</a>. A <a>shadow tree</a> is therefore never alone. The
2473: <a>node tree</a> of a <a for=/>shadow root</a>'s <a for=DocumentFragment>host</a> is sometimes
2474: referred to as the <dfn export id=concept-light-tree>light tree</dfn>.
2475: 
2476: <p class=note>A <a>shadow tree</a>'s corresponding <a>light tree</a> can be a <a>shadow tree</a>
2477: itself.
2478: 
2479: <p id=in-a-shadow-including-document>A <a for=/>node</a> is <dfn export>connected</dfn> if its
2480: <a>shadow-including root</a> is a <a for=/>document</a>.
2481: 
2695: 
2696: <div algorithm>
2697: <p>To <dfn>assign a slot</dfn>, given a <a>slottable</a> <var>slottable</var>:
2698: 
2699: <ol>
2700:  <li><p>Let <var>slot</var> be the result of <a>finding a slot</a> with <var>slottable</var>.
2701: 
2702:  <li><p>If <var>slot</var> is non-null, then run <a>assign slottables</a> for <var>slot</var>.
2703: </ol>
2704: </div>
2705: 
2706: <h5 id=signaling-slot-change>Signaling slot change</h5>
2707: 
2708: <p>Each <a>similar-origin window agent</a> has <dfn noexport id=signal-slot-list>signal slots</dfn>
2709: (a <a for=/>set</a> of <a>slots</a>), which is initially empty. [[!HTML]]
2710: 
2711: <div algorithm>
2712: <p>To <dfn>signal a slot change</dfn>, for a <a>slot</a> <var>slot</var>:
2713: 
2714: <ol>
2715:  <li><p><a for=set>Append</a> <var>slot</var> to <var>slot</var>'s <a>relevant agent</a>'s
2716:  <a>signal slots</a>.
2717: 
2718:  <li><p><a>Queue a mutation observer microtask</a>.
2719: </ol>
2720: </div>
2721: 
2722: 
2723: <h4 id=mutation-algorithms>Mutation algorithms</h4>
2724: 
2725: <div algorithm>
2726: <p>To <dfn id=concept-node-ensure-pre-insertion-validity>ensure pre-insert validity</dfn> given a
2727: <a for=/>node</a> <var>node</var>, a <a for=/>node</a> <var>parent</var>, null or a
2728: <a for=/>node</a> <var>child</var>, and a <a for=/>list</a> of <a for=/>nodes</a>
2729: <var>childrenToExclude</var>:
2730: 
2731: <ol>
2732:  <li><p>If <var>parent</var> is not a {{Document}}, {{DocumentFragment}}, or {{Element}}
2733:  <a for=/>node</a>, then <a>throw</a> a "{{HierarchyRequestError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
2734: 
2735:  <li><p>If <var>node</var> is a <a>host-including inclusive ancestor</a> of <var>parent</var>, then
2736:  <a>throw</a> a "{{HierarchyRequestError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
2737: 
2738:  <li><p>If <var>child</var> is non-null and its <a for=tree>parent</a> is not <var>parent</var>,
2739:  then <a>throw</a> a "{{NotFoundError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
2740: 
2741:  <li><p>If <var>node</var> is not a {{DocumentFragment}}, {{DocumentType}}, {{Element}}, or
2742:  {{CharacterData}} <a for=/>node</a>, then <a>throw</a> a
2743:  "{{HierarchyRequestError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
2744: 
2745:  <li>
2746:   <p>If <var>parent</var> is not a <a for=/>document</a>:
2747: 
2748:   <ol>
2749:    <li><p>If <var>node</var> is a <a>doctype</a>, then <a>throw</a> a
2750:    "{{HierarchyRequestError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
2751: 
2752:    <li><p>Return.
2753:   </ol>
2754: 
2755:  <li><p>If <var>node</var> is a {{Text}} <a for=/>node</a>, then <a>throw</a> a
2756:  "{{HierarchyRequestError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
2757: 
2758:  <li><p>If <var>node</var> is a {{CharacterData}} <a for=/>node</a>, then return.
2759: 
2760:  <li>
2761:   <p>If <var>node</var> is a {{DocumentFragment}} <a for=/>node</a>:
2762: 
2763:   <ol>
2764:    <li><p>If <var>node</var> has more than one <a for=/>element</a> <a for=tree>child</a> or has a
2765:    {{Text}} <a for=/>node</a> <a for=tree>child</a>, then <a>throw</a> a
2766:    "{{HierarchyRequestError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
2767: 
2768:    <li><p>If <var>node</var> has no <a for=/>element</a> <a for=tree>child</a>, then return.
2769:   </ol>
2770: 
2771:  <li>
2772:   <p>If <var>node</var> is a {{DocumentFragment}} or {{Element}} <a for=/>node</a>:
2773: 
2774:   <ol>
2775:    <li>
2776:     <p>If any of the following are true:
2777: 
2778:     <ul>
2779:      <li><p><var>parent</var> has an <a for=/>element</a> <a for=tree>child</a> that
2780:      <var>childrenToExclude</var> does not <a for=list>contain</a>;
2781: 
2782:      <li><p><var>child</var> is non-null and a <a>doctype</a> is <a>following</a> <var>child</var>;
2783:      or
2784: 
2785:      <li><p><var>child</var> is a <a>doctype</a> that <var>childrenToExclude</var> does not
2786:      <a for=list>contain</a>,
2787:     </ul>
2788: 
2789:     <p>then <a>throw</a> a "{{HierarchyRequestError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
2790: 
2791:    <li><p>Return.
2792:   </ol>
2793: 
2794:  <li><p><a for=/>Assert</a>: <var>node</var> is a <a>doctype</a>.
2795: 
2796:  <li>
2797:   <p>If any of the following are true:
2798: 
2799:   <ul>
2800:    <li><p><var>parent</var> has a <a>doctype</a> <a for=tree>child</a> that
2801:    <var>childrenToExclude</var> does not <a for=list>contain</a>;
2802: 
2803:    <li><p><var>child</var> is non-null and an <a for=/>element</a> is <a>preceding</a>
2804:    <var>child</var>; or
2805: 
2806:    <li><p><var>child</var> is null and <var>parent</var> has an <a for=/>element</a>
2807:    <a for=tree>child</a> that <var>childrenToExclude</var> does not <a for=list>contain</a>,
2808:   </ul>
2809: 
2810:   <p>then <a>throw</a> a "{{HierarchyRequestError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
2811: </ol>
2812: </div>
2813: 
2814: <div algorithm>
2815: <p>To <dfn export id=concept-node-pre-insert>pre-insert</dfn> a <a for=/>node</a> <var>node</var>
2816: into a <a for=/>node</a> <var>parent</var> before null or <a for=/>node</a> <var>child</var>:
2817: 
2818: <ol>
2819:  <li><p><a>Ensure pre-insert validity</a> given <var>node</var>, <var>parent</var>,
2820:  <var>child</var>, and « ».
2821: 
2822:  <li><p>Let <var>referenceChild</var> be <var>child</var>.
2823: 
2824:  <li><p>If <var>referenceChild</var> is <var>node</var>, then set <var>referenceChild</var> to
2825:  <var>node</var>'s <a for=tree>next sibling</a>.
2826: 
2827:  <li><p><a for=/>Insert</a> <var>node</var> into <var>parent</var> before <var>referenceChild</var>.
2828: 
2829:  <li><p>Return <var>node</var>.
2830:  <!-- Technically this is post-insert. -->
2831: </ol>
2832: </div>
2880:   </li>
2881:  </ol>
2882: </div>
2883: 
2884: <!-- See https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/34#issuecomment-125571750 for why we might need to
2885:      adjust this further based on the requirements of the script element. There might be other ways
2886:      to define that though as Olli suggests, so leaving that out for now. -->
2887: 
2888: <div algorithm>
2889: <p><a lt="Other applicable specifications">Specifications</a> may also define
2890: <dfn export id=concept-node-post-connection-ext>post-connection steps</dfn> for all or some
2891: <a for=/>nodes</a>. The algorithm is passed <var ignore>connectedNode</var>, as indicated in the
2892: <a for=/>insert</a> algorithm below.
2893: 
2894: <p class=note>The purpose of the <a>post-connection steps</a> is to provide an opportunity for
2895: <a for=/>nodes</a> to perform any connection-related operations that modify the <a>node tree</a>
2896: that <var ignore>connectedNode</var> <a>participates</a> in, create <a for=/>browsing contexts</a>,
2897: or otherwise execute JavaScript. These steps allow a batch of <a>nodes</a> to be
2898: <a for=/>inserted</a> <em>atomically</em> with respect to script, with all major side effects
2899: occurring <em>after</em> the batch insertions into the <a>node tree</a> is complete. This ensures
2900: that all pending <a>node tree</a> insertions completely finish before more insertions can occur.
2901: </div>
2902: 
2903: <div algorithm>
2904: <p><a lt="other applicable specifications">Specifications</a> may define
2905: <dfn export id=concept-node-children-changed-ext>children changed steps</dfn> for all or some
2906: <a for=/>nodes</a>. The algorithm is passed no argument and is called from <a for=/>insert</a>,
2907: <a for=/>remove</a>, and <a for=/>replace data</a>.
2908: </div>
2909: 
2910: <div algorithm=insert>
2911: <p>To <dfn export id=concept-node-insert>insert</dfn> a <a for=/>node</a> <var>node</var> into a
2912: <a for=/>node</a> <var>parent</var> before null or a <a for=/>node</a> <var>child</var>, with an
2913: optional boolean <dfn for="insert"><var>suppressObservers</var></dfn> (default false):
2914: 
2915: <ol>
2916:  <li><p>Let <var>nodes</var> be <var>node</var>'s <a for=tree>children</a>, if <var>node</var> is a
2917:  {{DocumentFragment}} <a for=/>node</a>; otherwise « <var>node</var> ».
2918: 
2919:  <li><p>Let <var>count</var> be <var>nodes</var>'s <a for=set>size</a>.
2920: 
2921:  <li><p>If <var>count</var> is 0, then return.
2922: 
2923:  <li>
2924:   <p>If <var>node</var> is a {{DocumentFragment}} <a for=/>node</a>:
2925: 
2926:   <ol>
2927:    <li><p><a for=/>Remove</a> its <a for=tree>children</a> with
2928:    <a for=remove><i>suppressObservers</i></a> set to true.
2929: 
2930:    <li>
2931:     <p><a>Queue a tree mutation record</a> for <var>node</var> with « », <var>nodes</var>, null, and
2932:     null.
2933: 
2934:     <p class=note>This step intentionally does not pay attention to <var>suppressObservers</var>.
2935:   </ol>
2936: 
2937:  <li>
2938:   <p>If <var>child</var> is non-null:
2939: 
2940:   <ol>
2941:    <li><p>For each <a>live range</a> whose <a for=range>start node</a> is <var>parent</var> and
2942:    <a for=range>start offset</a> is greater than <var>child</var>'s <a for=tree>index</a>: increase
2943:    its <a for=range>start offset</a> by <var>count</var>.
2944: 
2945:    <li><p>For each <a>live range</a> whose <a for=range>end node</a> is <var>parent</var> and
2946:    <a for=range>end offset</a> is greater than <var>child</var>'s <a for=tree>index</a>: increase
2947:    its <a for=range>end offset</a> by <var>count</var>.
2948:   </ol>
2949: 
2950:  <li><p>Let <var>previousSibling</var> be <var>child</var>'s <a>previous sibling</a> or
2951:  <var>parent</var>'s <a>last child</a> if <var>child</var> is null.
2952: 
2953:  <li>
2954:   <p>For each <var>node</var> in <var>nodes</var>, in <a>tree order</a>:
2955: 
2956:   <ol>
2957:    <li><p><a>Adopt</a> <var>node</var> into <var>parent</var>'s <a for=Node>node document</a>.
2958: 
2959:    <li><p>If <var>child</var> is null, then <a for=set>append</a> <var>node</var> to
2960:    <var>parent</var>'s <a for=tree>children</a>.
2961: 
2962:    <li><p>Otherwise, <a for=set>insert</a> <var>node</var> into <var>parent</var>'s
2963:    <a for=tree>children</a> before <var>child</var>'s <a for=tree>index</a>.
2964: 
2965:    <li><p>If <var>parent</var> is a <a for=Element>shadow host</a> whose <a for=/>shadow root</a>'s
2966:    <a for=ShadowRoot>slot assignment</a> is "<code>named</code>" and <var>node</var> is a
2967:    <a>slottable</a>, then <a>assign a slot</a> for <var>node</var>.
2968: 
2969:    <li><p>If <var>parent</var>'s <a for=tree>root</a> is a <a for=/>shadow root</a>, and
2970:    <var>parent</var> is a <a>slot</a> whose <a for=slot>assigned nodes</a> is the empty list,
2971:    then run <a>signal a slot change</a> for <var>parent</var>.
2972: 
2973:    <li><p>Run <a>assign slottables for a tree</a> with <var>node</var>'s <a for=tree>root</a>.
2974: 
2975:    <li>
2976:     <p>For each <a>shadow-including inclusive descendant</a> <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> of
2977:     <var>node</var>, in <a>shadow-including tree order</a>:
2978: 
2979:     <ol>
2980:      <li><p>Run the <a>insertion steps</a> with <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>.
2981: 
2982:      <li><p>If <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> is not <a>connected</a>, then
2983:      <a for=iteration>continue</a>.
2984: 
2985:      <li>
2986:       <p>If <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> is an <a for=/>element</a> and
2987:       <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=Element>custom element registry</a> is non-null:
2988: 
2989:       <ol>
2990:        <li><p>If <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=Element>custom element registry</a>'s
2991:        <a for=CustomElementRegistry>is scoped</a> is true, then <a for=set>append</a>
2992:        <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=Node>node document</a> to
2993:        <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=Element>custom element registry</a>'s
2994:        <a for=CustomElementRegistry>scoped document set</a>.
2995: 
2996:        <li><p>If <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> is <a for=Element>custom</a>, then
2997:        <a>enqueue a custom element callback reaction</a> with <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>,
2998:        callback name "<code>connectedCallback</code>", and « ».
2999: 
3000:        <li>
3001:         <p>Otherwise, <a lt="try to upgrade an element">try to upgrade</a>
3002:         <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>.
3003: 
3004:         <p class=note>If this successfully upgrades <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>, its
3005:         <code>connectedCallback</code> will be enqueued automatically during the
3006:         <a>upgrade an element</a> algorithm.
3007:       </ol>
3008: 
3009:      <li><p>Otherwise, if <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> is a <a for=/>shadow root</a>,
3010:      <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>custom element registry</a> is non-null, and
3011:      <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>custom element registry</a>'s
3012:      <a for=CustomElementRegistry>is scoped</a> is true, then <a for=set>append</a>
3013:      <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=Node>node document</a> to
3014:      <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>custom element registry</a>'s
3015:      <a for=CustomElementRegistry>scoped document set</a>.
3016:     </ol>
3017:   </ol>
3018: 
3019:  <li><p>If <var>suppressObservers</var> is false, then <a>queue a tree mutation record</a> for
3020:  <var>parent</var> with <var>nodes</var>, « », <var>previousSibling</var>, and <var>child</var>.
3021: 
3022:  <li><p>Run the <a>children changed steps</a> for <var>parent</var>.
3023: 
3024:  <li>
3025:   <p>Let <var>staticNodeList</var> be a <a for=/>list</a> of <a for=/>nodes</a>, initially « ».
3026: 
3027:   <p class="note">We collect all <a for=/>nodes</a> <em>before</em> calling the
3028:   <a>post-connection steps</a> on any one of them, instead of calling the
3029:   <a>post-connection steps</a> <em>while</em> we're traversing the <a>node tree</a>. This is because
3030:   the <a>post-connection steps</a> can modify the tree's structure, making live traversal unsafe,
3031:   possibly leading to the <a>post-connection steps</a> being called multiple times on the same
3032:   <a for=/>node</a>.
3033:  </li>
3034: 
3035:  <li>
3036:   <p>For each <var>node</var> of <var>nodes</var>, in <a>tree order</a>:
3037: 
3038:   <ol>
3039:    <li><p>For each <a>shadow-including inclusive descendant</a> <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> of
3040:    <var>node</var>, in <a>shadow-including tree order</a>: <a for=list>append</a>
3041:    <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> to <var>staticNodeList</var>.
3042:   </ol>
3043:  </li>
3044: 
3045:  <li><p><a for=list>For each</a> <var>node</var> of <var>staticNodeList</var>: if <var>node</var> is
3046:  <a>connected</a>, then run the <a>post-connection steps</a> with <var>node</var>.
3047: </ol>
3048: </div>
3175: 
3176:   <ol>
3177:    <li><p>Let <var>isSubtreeRoot</var> be true if <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> is
3178:    <var>node</var>; otherwise false.
3179: 
3180:    <li>
3181:     <p>Run the <a>moving steps</a> with <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>, <var>isSubtreeRoot</var>,
3182:     and <var>oldParent</var>.
3183: 
3184:     <p class="note">Because the <a>move</a> algorithm is a separate primitive from
3185:     <a for=/>insert</a> and <a for=/>remove</a>, it does not invoke the <a>insertion steps</a>
3186:     or <a>removing steps</a> for <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>.
3187:    </li>
3188: 
3189:    <li><p>If <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> is <a for=Element>custom</a> and <var>newParent</var> is
3190:    <a>connected</a>, then <a>enqueue a custom element callback reaction</a> with
3191:    <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>, callback name "<code>connectedMoveCallback</code>", and « ».
3192:   </ol>
3193:  </li>
3194: 
3195:  <li><p><a>Queue a tree mutation record</a> for <var>oldParent</var> with « », « <var>node</var> »,
3196:  <var>oldPreviousSibling</var>, and <var>oldNextSibling</var>.
3197: 
3198:  <li><p><a>Queue a tree mutation record</a> for <var>newParent</var> with « <var>node</var> », « »,
3199:  <var>newPreviousSibling</var>, and <var>child</var>.
3200: </ol>
3201: </div>
3202: 
3203: <hr>
3204: 
3205: <div algorithm>
3206: <p>To <dfn export id=concept-node-replace>replace</dfn> a <a for=/>node</a> <var>child</var> with
3207: a <a for=/>node</a> <var>node</var> within a <a for=/>node</a> <var>parent</var>:
3208: 
3209: <ol>
3210:  <li><p><a>Ensure pre-insert validity</a> given <var>node</var>, <var>parent</var>,
3211:  <var>child</var>, and « <var>child</var> ».
3212: 
3213:  <li><p>Let <var>referenceChild</var> be <var>child</var>'s <a for=tree>next sibling</a>.
3214: 
3215:  <li><p>If <var>referenceChild</var> is <var>node</var>, then set <var>referenceChild</var> to
3216:  <var>node</var>'s <a for=tree>next sibling</a>.
3217: 
3218:  <li><p>Let <var>previousSibling</var> be <var>child</var>'s <a>previous sibling</a>.
3219: 
3220:  <li><p>Let <var>removedNodes</var> be the empty set.
3221: 
3222:  <li><p><a>Adopt</a> <var>node</var> into <var>parent</var>'s <a for=Node>node document</a>.
3223: 
3224:  <li>
3225:   <p>If <var>child</var>'s <a for=tree>parent</a> is non-null:
3226: 
3227:   <ol>
3228:    <li><p>Set <var>removedNodes</var> to « <var>child</var> ».
3229: 
3230:    <li><p><a for=/>Remove</a> <var>child</var> with <a for=remove><i>suppressObservers</i></a> set
3231:    to true.
3232:   </ol>
3233: 
3234:   <p class=note>The above can only be false if <var>child</var> is <var>node</var>.
3235: 
3236:  <li><p>Let <var>nodes</var> be <var>node</var>'s <a for=tree>children</a> if <var>node</var> is a
3237:  {{DocumentFragment}} <a for=/>node</a>; otherwise « <var>node</var> ».
3238:  <!-- This needs to come before insert as that removes the children of a
3239:       DocumentFragment node. -->
3240: 
3241:  <li><p><a for=/>Insert</a> <var>node</var> into <var>parent</var> before <var>referenceChild</var>
3242:  with <a for=insert><i>suppressObservers</i></a> set to true.
3243: 
3244:  <li><p><a>Queue a tree mutation record</a> for <var>parent</var> with <var>nodes</var>,
3245:  <var>removedNodes</var>, <var>previousSibling</var>, and <var>referenceChild</var>.
3246: 
3247:  <li><p>Return <var>child</var>.
3248: </ol>
3249: </div>
3252: <p>To <dfn export for=Node id=concept-node-replace-all>replace all</dfn> with a <a for=/>node</a> or
3253: null <var>node</var> within a <a for=/>node</a> <var>parent</var>:
3254: 
3255: <ol>
3256:  <li><p>Let <var>removedNodes</var> be <var>parent</var>'s <a for=tree>children</a>.
3257: 
3258:  <li><p>Let <var>addedNodes</var> be the empty set.
3259: 
3260:  <li><p>If <var>node</var> is a {{DocumentFragment}} <a for=/>node</a>, then set
3261:  <var>addedNodes</var> to <var>node</var>'s <a for=tree>children</a>.
3262: 
3263:  <li><p>Otherwise, if <var>node</var> is non-null, set <var>addedNodes</var> to « <var>node</var> ».
3264: 
3265:  <li><p><a for=/>Remove</a> all <var>parent</var>'s <a for=tree>children</a>, in <a>tree order</a>,
3266:  with <a for=remove><i>suppressObservers</i></a> set to true.
3267: 
3268:  <li><p>If <var>node</var> is non-null, then <a for=/>insert</a> <var>node</var> into
3269:  <var>parent</var> before null with <a for=insert><i>suppressObservers</i></a> set to true.
3270: 
3271:  <li><p>If either <var>addedNodes</var> or <var>removedNodes</var> <a for=set>is not empty</a>,
3272:  then <a>queue a tree mutation record</a> for <var>parent</var> with <var>addedNodes</var>,
3273:  <var>removedNodes</var>, null, and null.
3274: </ol>
3275: 
3276: <p class=note>This algorithm does not make any checks with regards to the
3277: <a>node tree</a> constraints. Specification authors need to use it wisely.
3278: </div>
3279: 
3280: <hr>
3281: 
3282: <div algorithm>
3283: <p>To <dfn export id=concept-node-pre-remove>pre-remove</dfn> a <a for=/>node</a> <var>child</var>
3284: from a <a for=/>node</a> <var>parent</var>:
3285: 
3286: <ol>
3287:  <li><p>If <var>child</var>'s <a for=tree>parent</a> is not <var>parent</var>, then <a>throw</a> a
3288:  "{{NotFoundError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
3289: 
3290:  <li><p><a for=/>Remove</a> <var>child</var>.
3291: 
3292:  <li><p>Return <var>child</var>.
3293:  <!-- Technically this is post-remove. -->
3294: </ol>
3295: </div>
3296: 
3297: <div algorithm>
3298: <p><a lt="Other applicable specifications">Specifications</a> may define
3299: <dfn export id=concept-node-remove-ext>removing steps</dfn> for all or some <a for=/>nodes</a>. The
3300: algorithm is passed a <a for=/>node</a> <var ignore>removedNode</var>, a boolean
3301: <var ignore>isSubtreeRoot</var>, and a <a for=/>node</a> <var ignore>oldAncestor</var> as indicated
3302: in the <a for=/>remove</a> algorithm below.
3303: </div>
3304: 
3305: <div algorithm=remove>
3306: <p>To <dfn export id=concept-node-remove>remove</dfn> a <a for=/>node</a> <var>node</var>, with an
3307: optional boolean <dfn for=remove><var>suppressObservers</var></dfn> (default false):
3308: 
3309: <ol>
3310:  <li><p>Let <var>parent</var> be <var>node</var>'s <a for=tree>parent</a>.
3311: 
3312:  <li><p>Assert: <var>parent</var> is non-null.
3313: 
3314:  <li><p>Run the <a>live range pre-remove steps</a>, given <var>node</var>.
3315: 
3316:  <li><p>For each {{NodeIterator}} object <var>iterator</var> whose
3317:  <a for=traversal>root</a>'s <a for=Node>node document</a> is <var>node</var>'s
3318:  <a for=Node>node document</a>: run the <a><code>NodeIterator</code> pre-remove steps</a> given
3319:  <var>node</var> and <var>iterator</var>.
3320: 
3321:  <li><p>Let <var>oldPreviousSibling</var> be <var>node</var>'s <a>previous sibling</a>.
3322: 
3323:  <li><p>Let <var>oldNextSibling</var> be <var>node</var>'s <a for=tree>next sibling</a>.
3324: 
3325:  <li><p><a for=set>Remove</a> <var>node</var> from its <var>parent</var>'s <a for=tree>children</a>.
3326: 
3327:  <li><p>If <var>node</var> is <a for=slottable>assigned</a>, then run <a>assign slottables</a> for
3328:  <var>node</var>'s <a>assigned slot</a>.
3329: 
3330:  <li><p>If <var>parent</var>'s <a for=tree>root</a> is a <a for=/>shadow root</a>, and
3331:  <var>parent</var> is a <a>slot</a> whose <a for=slot>assigned nodes</a> is the empty list,
3332:  then run <a>signal a slot change</a> for <var>parent</var>.
3333: 
3334:  <li>
3335:   <p>If <var>node</var> has an <a>inclusive descendant</a> that is a <a>slot</a>:
3336: 
3337:   <ol>
3338:    <li><p>Run <a>assign slottables for a tree</a> with <var>parent</var>'s <a for=tree>root</a>.
3339: 
3340:    <li><p>Run <a>assign slottables for a tree</a> with <var>node</var>.
3341:   </ol>
3342: 
3343:  <li><p>Run the <a>removing steps</a> with <var>node</var>, true, and <var>parent</var>.
3344: 
3345:  <li><p>Let <var>isParentConnected</var> be <var>parent</var>'s <a>connected</a>.
3346: 
3347:  <li>
3348:   <p>If <var>node</var> is <a for=Element>custom</a> and <var>isParentConnected</var> is true, then
3349:   <a>enqueue a custom element callback reaction</a> with <var>node</var>, callback name
3350:   "<code>disconnectedCallback</code>", and « ».
3351: 
3352:   <p class=note>It is intentional for now that <a for=Element>custom</a> <a for=/>elements</a> do
3353:   not get <var>parent</var> passed. This might change in the future if there is a need.
3354: 
3355:  <li>
3356:   <p>For each <a>shadow-including descendant</a> <var>descendant</var> of <var>node</var>, in
3357:   <a>shadow-including tree order</a>:
3358: 
3359:   <ol>
3360:    <li><p>Run the <a>removing steps</a> with <var>descendant</var>, false, and <var>parent</var>.
3361: 
3362:    <li><p>If <var>descendant</var> is <a for=Element>custom</a> and <var>isParentConnected</var>
3363:    is true, then <a>enqueue a custom element callback reaction</a> with <var>descendant</var>,
3364:    callback name "<code>disconnectedCallback</code>", and « ».
3365:   </ol>
3366:  </li>
3367: 
3368:  <li><p><a>Add transient registered observers</a> given <var>node</var> and <var>parent</var>.
3369: 
3370:  <li><p>If <var>suppressObservers</var> is false, then <a>queue a tree mutation record</a> for
3371:  <var>parent</var> with « », « <var>node</var> », <var>oldPreviousSibling</var>, and
3372:  <var>oldNextSibling</var>.
3373: 
3374:  <li><p>Run the <a>children changed steps</a> for <var>parent</var>.
3375: </ol>
3376: </div>
6167: <div algorithm>
6168: <p>The <dfn method for=Document><code>importNode(<var>node</var>, <var>options</var>)</code></dfn>
6169: method steps are:
6170: 
6171: <ol>
6172:  <li><p>If <var>node</var> is a <a for=/>document</a> or <a for=/>shadow root</a>, then <a>throw</a>
6173:  a "{{NotSupportedError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
6174: 
6175:  <li><p>Let <var>subtree</var> be false.
6176: 
6177:  <li><p>Let <var>registry</var> be null.
6178: 
6179:  <li><p>If <var>options</var> is a boolean, then set <var>subtree</var> to <var>options</var>.
6180: 
6181:  <li>
6182:   <p>Otherwise:
6183: 
6184:   <ol>
6185:    <li><p>Set <var>subtree</var> to the negation of
6186:    <var>options</var>["{{ImportNodeOptions/selfOnly}}"].
6187: 
6188:    <li><p>If <var>options</var>["{{ImportNodeOptions/customElementRegistry}}"]
6189:    <a for=map>exists</a>, then set <var>registry</var> to it.
6190: 
6191:    <li><p>If <var>registry</var>'s <a for=CustomElementRegistry>is scoped</a> is false and
6192:    <var>registry</var> is not <a>this</a>'s <a for=Document>custom element registry</a>, then
6193:    <a>throw</a> a "{{NotSupportedError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
6194:   </ol>
6195: 
6196:  <li><p>If <var>registry</var> is null, then set <var>registry</var> to the result of
6197:  <a for=/>looking up a custom element registry</a> given <a>this</a>.
6198: 
6199:  <li><p>Return the result of <a>cloning a node</a> given <var>node</var> with
6200:  <a for="clone a node"><i>document</i></a> set to <a>this</a>,
6201:  <a for="clone a node"><i>subtree</i></a> set to <var>subtree</var>, and
6202:  <a for="clone a node"><i>fallbackRegistry</i></a> set to <var>registry</var>.
6203: </ol>
6204: </div>
6205: 
6206: <div algorithm>
6207: <p><a lt="Other applicable specifications">Specifications</a> may define
6208: <dfn export id=concept-node-adopt-ext>adopting steps</dfn> for all or some <a for=/>nodes</a>. The
6209: algorithm is passed <var ignore>node</var> and <var ignore>oldDocument</var>, as indicated in the
6210: <a>adopt</a> algorithm.
6211: </div>
6212: 
6213: <div algorithm>
6214: <p>To <dfn export id=concept-node-adopt>adopt</dfn> a <a for=/>node</a> <var>node</var> into a
6215: <a for=/>document</a> <var>document</var>:
6216: 
6217: <ol>
6218:  <li><p>Let <var>oldDocument</var> be <var>node</var>'s <a for=Node>node document</a>.
6219: 
6220:  <li><p>If <var>node</var>'s <a for=tree>parent</a> is non-null, then <a for=/>remove</a>
6221:  <var>node</var>.
6222: 
6223:  <li>
6224:   <p>If <var>document</var> is not <var>oldDocument</var>, then for each
6225:   <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> of <var>node</var>'s <a>shadow-including inclusive descendants</a>,
6226:   in <a>shadow-including tree order</a>:
6227: 
6228:   <ol>
6229:    <li><p>Set <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=Node>node document</a> to <var>document</var>.
6230: 
6231:    <li>
6232:     <p>If <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> is a <a for=/>shadow root</a> and if any of the following
6233:     are true:
6234: 
6235:     <ul>
6236:      <li><p><var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>custom element registry</a> is null
6237:      and <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>keep custom element registry null</a> is
6238:      false; or
6239: 
6240:      <li><p><var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>custom element registry</a>
6241:      <a>is a global custom element registry</a>,
6242:     </ul>
6243: 
6244:     <p>then set <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>custom element registry</a> to
6245:     <var>document</var>'s <a for=Document>custom element registry</a>'s
6246:     <a>effective global custom element registry</a>.
6247: 
6248:    <li>
6249:     <p>Otherwise, if <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> is an <a for=/>element</a>:
6250: 
6251:     <ol>
6252:      <li><p>Set the <a for=Node>node document</a> of each <a>attribute</a> in
6253:      <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=Element>attribute list</a> to <var>document</var>.
6254: 
6255:      <li>
6256:       <p>If <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=Element>custom element registry</a> is null or
6257:       <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=Element>custom element registry</a>'s
6258:       <a for=CustomElementRegistry>is scoped</a> is false:
6259: 
6260:       <ol>
6261:        <li><p>Let <var>registry</var> be null.
6262: 
6263:        <li><p>If <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=Element>custom element registry</a> is
6264:        non-null, <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=tree>parent</a> is null, or
6265:        <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=tree>parent</a> is an
6266:        <a>exclusive <code>DocumentFragment</code> node</a>, then set <var>registry</var> to
6267:        <var>document</var>'s <a for=Document>custom element registry</a>.
6268: 
6269:        <li><p>Otherwise, set <var>registry</var> to the result of
6270:        <a for=/>looking up a custom element registry</a> given <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s
6271:        <a for=tree>parent</a>.
6272: 
6273:        <li><p>Set <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>'s <a for=Element>custom element registry</a> to
6274:        <var>registry</var>'s <a>effective global custom element registry</a>.
6275:       </ol>
6276: 
6277:      <li><p>If <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> is <a for=Element>custom</a>, then
6278:      <a>enqueue a custom element callback reaction</a> with <var>inclusiveDescendant</var>, callback
6279:      name "<code>adoptedCallback</code>", and « <var>oldDocument</var>, <var>document</var> ».
6280:      <!-- attributeChangedCallback is also old, then new -->
6281:     </ol>
6282: 
6283:    <li><p>Run the <a>adopting steps</a> with <var>inclusiveDescendant</var> and
6284:    <var>oldDocument</var>.
6285:   </ol>
6286: </ol>
6287: </div>
6288: 
6289: <div algorithm>
6290: <p>The <dfn method for=Document><code>adoptNode(<var>node</var>)</code></dfn> method steps are:
6291: 
6292: <ol>
6293:  <li><p>If <var>node</var> is a <a for=/>document</a>, then <a>throw</a> a
6294:  "{{NotSupportedError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
6295: 
6296:  <li><p>If <var>node</var> is a <a for=/>shadow root</a>, then <a>throw</a> a
6297:  "{{HierarchyRequestError!!exception}}" {{DOMException}}.
6298: 
6299:  <li><p><a>Adopt</a> <var>node</var> into <a>this</a>.
6300: 
6301:  <li><p>Return <var>node</var>.
6302: </ol>
6303: </div>
6304: 
6305: <hr>
6306: 
6307: <p>Null or a {{CustomElementRegistry}} object <var>registry</var>
6308: <dfn>is a global custom element registry</dfn> if <var>registry</var> is non-null and
6309: <var>registry</var>'s <a for=CustomElementRegistry>is scoped</a> is false.
6310: 
6311: <p>Null or a {{CustomElementRegistry}} object <var>registry</var>'s
6312: <dfn>effective global custom element registry</dfn> is:
6313: 
6314: <ol>
6315:  <li><p>If <var>registry</var> <a>is a global custom element registry</a>, then return
6316:  <var>registry</var>.
6317: 
6318:  <li><p>Return null.
6319: </ol>
6631: <dfn export id=concept-doctype-systemid for=DocumentType>system ID</dfn> (a string).
6632: 
6633: <div algorithm>
6634: <p>To <dfn export>create a doctype</dfn> given a <a for=/>document</a> <var>document</var>, a string
6635: <var>name</var>, and optionally a string <var>publicId</var> (default the empty string) and a string
6636: <var>systemId</var> (default the empty string):
6637: 
6638: <ol>
6639:  <li><p>Let <var>doctype</var> be the result of <a>creating a node</a> that implements
6640:  {{DocumentType}}, given <var>document</var>.
6641: 
6642:  <li><p>Set <var>doctype</var>'s <a for=DocumentType>name</a> to <var>name</var>, <a>public ID</a> to
6643:  <var>publicId</var>, and <a>system ID</a> to <var>systemId</var>.
6644: 
6645:  <li><p>Return <var>doctype</var>.
6646: </ol>
6647: </div>
6648: 
6649: <p>The <dfn attribute for=DocumentType><code>name</code></dfn> getter steps are to return
6650: <a>this</a>'s <a for=DocumentType>name</a>.
6651: 
6652: <p>The <dfn attribute for=DocumentType><code>publicId</code></dfn> getter steps are to return
6653: <a>this</a>'s <a>public ID</a>.
6654: 
6655: <p>The <dfn attribute for=DocumentType><code>systemId</code></dfn> getter steps are to return
6656: <a>this</a>'s <a>system ID</a>.
6657: 
6658: 
6659: <h3 id=interface-documentfragment>Interface {{DocumentFragment}}</h3>
6660: 
6661: <pre class=idl>
6662: [Exposed=Window]
6663: interface DocumentFragment : Node {
6664:   constructor();
6665: };
6666: </pre>
6667: 
6668: <dl class=domintro>
6669:  <dt><code><var ignore>tree</var> = new {{DocumentFragment()}}</code>
6670:  <dd>Returns a new {{DocumentFragment}} <a for=/>node</a>.
6671: </dl>
6672: 
6673: <hr>
6674: 
6675: <div algorithm>
6676: <p>An <dfn export>exclusive {{DocumentFragment}} node</dfn> is a {{DocumentFragment}}
6677: <a for=/>node</a> that is not a {{ShadowRoot}} <a for=/>node</a>.
6678: </div>
6679: 
6680: <p>A {{DocumentFragment}} <a for=/>node</a> has an associated
6681: <dfn export id=concept-documentfragment-host for=DocumentFragment>host</dfn> (null or an
6682: <a for=/>element</a> in a different <a>node tree</a>). It is null unless otherwise stated.
6683: 
6684: <div algorithm>
6685: <p>An object <var>A</var> is a
6686: <dfn export id=concept-tree-host-including-inclusive-ancestor>host-including inclusive ancestor</dfn>
6687: of an object <var>B</var>, if either <var>A</var> is an <a for=tree>inclusive ancestor</a> of <var>B</var>,
6688: or if <var>B</var>'s <a for=tree>root</a> has a non-null <a for=DocumentFragment>host</a> and
6689: <var>A</var> is a <a>host-including inclusive ancestor</a> of <var>B</var>'s <a for=tree>root</a>'s
6690: <a for=DocumentFragment>host</a>.
6691: </div>
6692: 
6693: <p class=note>The {{DocumentFragment}} <a for=/>node</a>'s <a for=DocumentFragment>host</a>
6694: concept is useful for HTML's <{template}> element and for <a for=/>shadow roots</a>, and impacts the
6695: <a>pre-insert</a> and <a>replace</a> algorithms.
6696: 
6697: <div algorithm>
6698: <p>To <dfn export>create a document fragment</dfn> given a <a for=/>document</a>
6699: <var>document</var>: return the result of <a>creating a node</a> that implements
6700: {{DocumentFragment}}, given <var>document</var>.
6701: </div>
6702: 
6703: <div algorithm>
6704: <p>The
6705: <dfn constructor for=DocumentFragment lt=DocumentFragment()><code>new DocumentFragment()</code></dfn>
6706: constructor steps are to set <a>this</a>'s <a for=Node>node document</a> to
6707: <a>current global object</a>'s <a>associated <code>Document</code></a>.
6708: </div>
6709: 
6710: 
6711: <h3 id=interface-shadowroot>Interface {{ShadowRoot}}</h3>
6712: 
6713: <pre class=idl>
6714: [Exposed=Window]
6715: interface ShadowRoot : DocumentFragment {
6716:   readonly attribute ShadowRootMode mode;
6717:   readonly attribute boolean delegatesFocus;
6718:   readonly attribute boolean serializable;
6719:   readonly attribute SlotAssignmentMode slotAssignment;
6720:   readonly attribute boolean clonable;
6721:   readonly attribute Element host;
6722: 
6723:   attribute EventHandler onslotchange;
6724: };
6725: 
6726: enum ShadowRootMode { "open", "closed" };
6727: enum SlotAssignmentMode { "manual", "named" };
6728: </pre>
6729: 
6730: <p>{{ShadowRoot}} <a for=/>nodes</a> are simply known as
6731: <dfn export id=concept-shadow-root lt="shadow root">shadow roots</dfn>.
6732: 
6733: <p><a for=/>Shadow roots</a>'s associated <a for=DocumentFragment>host</a> is never null.
6734: <!-- If we ever change this, e.g., add a ShadowRoot object constructor, that would have serious
6735:      consequences for innerHTML. -->
6736: 
6737: <p><a for=/>Shadow roots</a> have an associated <dfn for=ShadowRoot>mode</dfn> ("<code>open</code>"
6738: or "<code>closed</code>").
6739: 
6740: <p><a for=/>Shadow roots</a> have an associated <dfn export for=ShadowRoot>delegates focus</dfn>
6741: (a boolean). It is initially set to false.
6742: 
6743: <p><a for=/>Shadow roots</a> have an associated
6744: <dfn export for=ShadowRoot>available to element internals</dfn> (a boolean). It is initially set to
6745: false.
6746: 
6747: <p><a for=/>Shadow roots</a> have an associated <dfn export for=ShadowRoot>declarative</dfn>
6748: (a boolean). It is initially set to false.
6749: 
6750: <p><a for=/>Shadow roots</a> have an associated <dfn for=ShadowRoot>serializable</dfn> (a boolean).
6751: It is initially set to false.
6752: 
6753: <p><a for=/>Shadow roots</a> have an associated <dfn for=ShadowRoot>slot assignment</dfn>
6754: ("<code>manual</code>" or "<code>named</code>").
6755: 
6756: <p><a for=/>Shadow roots</a> have an associated <dfn for=ShadowRoot>clonable</dfn> (a boolean).
6757: It is initially set to false.
6758: 
6759: <p><a for=/>Shadow roots</a> have an associated <dfn for=ShadowRoot>custom element registry</dfn>
6760: (null or a {{CustomElementRegistry}} object). It is initially null.
6761: 
6762: <p><a for=/>Shadow roots</a> have an associated
6763: <dfn for=ShadowRoot>keep custom element registry null</dfn> (a boolean). It is initially false.
6764: 
6765: <p class=note>This can only ever be true in combination with declarative shadow roots. And it only
6766: matters for as long as the <a for=/>shadow root</a>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>custom element registry</a>
6767: is null.
6768: 
6769: <hr>
6770: 
6771: <p>A <a for=/>shadow root</a>'s <a>get the parent</a> algorithm, given an <var>event</var>, returns
6772: null if <var>event</var>'s <a>composed flag</a> is unset and <a for=/>shadow root</a> is the
6773: <a for=tree>root</a> of <var>event</var>'s <a for=Event>path</a>'s first <a>event path item</a>'s
6774: <a for="event path item">invocation target</a>; otherwise <a for=/>shadow root</a>'s
6775: <a for=DocumentFragment>host</a>.
6776: 
6777: <hr>
6778: 
6779: <p>The <dfn attribute for=ShadowRoot><code>mode</code></dfn> getter steps are to return
6780: <a>this</a>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>mode</a>.
6781: 
6782: <p>The <dfn attribute for=ShadowRoot><code>delegatesFocus</code></dfn> getter steps are to return
6783: <a>this</a>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>delegates focus</a>.
6784: 
6785: <p>The <dfn attribute for=ShadowRoot><code>serializable</code></dfn> getter steps are to return
6786: <a>this</a>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>serializable</a>.
6787: 
6788: <p>The <dfn attribute for=ShadowRoot><code>slotAssignment</code></dfn> getter steps are to return
6789: <a>this</a>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>slot assignment</a>.
6790: 
6791: <p>The <dfn attribute for=ShadowRoot><code>clonable</code></dfn> getter steps are to return
6792: <a>this</a>'s <a for=ShadowRoot>clonable</a>.
6793: 
6794: <p>The <dfn attribute for=ShadowRoot><code>host</code></dfn> getter steps are to return
6795: <a>this</a>'s <a for=DocumentFragment>host</a>.
6796: 
6797: <hr>
6798: 
6799: <p>The <dfn attribute for=ShadowRoot><code>onslotchange</code></dfn> attribute is an
6800: <a>event handler IDL attribute</a> for the
6801: <dfn for=ShadowRoot export><code>onslotchange</code></dfn> <a>event handler</a>, whose
6802: <a>event handler event type</a> is {{HTMLSlotElement/slotchange}}.
6803: 
6804: <hr>
6805: 
6806: <p>In <dfn export id=concept-shadow-including-tree-order>shadow-including tree order</dfn> is
6807: <a>shadow-including preorder, depth-first traversal</a> of a <a>node tree</a>.
6808: <dfn noexport>Shadow-including preorder, depth-first traversal</dfn> of a <a>node tree</a>
6809: <var>tree</var> is preorder, depth-first traversal of <var>tree</var>, with for each
6810: <a for=Element>shadow host</a> encountered in <var>tree</var>,
6811: <a>shadow-including preorder, depth-first traversal</a> of that <a for=/>element</a>'s
6812: <a for=Element>shadow root</a>'s <a>node tree</a> just after it is encountered.
6813: 
6814: <p>The <dfn export id=concept-shadow-including-root>shadow-including root</dfn> of an object is its
6815: <a for=tree>root</a>'s <a for=DocumentFragment>host</a>'s <a>shadow-including root</a>, if the
6816: object's <a for=tree>root</a> is a <a for=/>shadow root</a>; otherwise its <a for=tree>root</a>.
6817: 
6818: <p>An object <var>A</var> is a
6819: <dfn export id=concept-shadow-including-descendant>shadow-including descendant</dfn> of an object
6820: <var>B</var>, if <var>A</var> is a <a for=tree>descendant</a> of <var>B</var>, or <var>A</var>'s
6821: <a for=tree>root</a> is a <a for=/>shadow root</a> and <var>A</var>'s <a for=tree>root</a>'s
6822: <a for=DocumentFragment>host</a> is a <a>shadow-including inclusive descendant</a> of <var>B</var>.
6823: 
6824: <p>A
6825: <dfn export id=concept-shadow-including-inclusive-descendant>shadow-including inclusive descendant</dfn>
6826: is an object or one of its <a>shadow-including descendants</a>.
6827: 
6828: <p>An object <var>A</var> is a
6829: <dfn export id=concept-shadow-including-ancestor>shadow-including ancestor</dfn> of an object
6830: <var>B</var>, if and only if <var>B</var> is a <a>shadow-including descendant</a> of <var>A</var>.
6831: 
6832: <p>A
6833: <dfn export id=concept-shadow-including-inclusive-ancestor>shadow-including inclusive ancestor</dfn>
6834: is an object or one of its <a>shadow-including ancestors</a>.
6966: </dl>
6967: 
6968: <p>When an <a for=/>element</a> is <a lt="create an element">created</a>, all of these values are
6969: initialized.
6970: 
6971: <p>An <a for=/>element</a> whose <a for=Element>custom element state</a> is
6972: "<code>uncustomized</code>" or "<code>custom</code>" is said to be
6973: <dfn export id=concept-element-defined for=Element>defined</dfn>. An <a for=/>element</a> whose
6974: <a for=Element>custom element state</a> is "<code>custom</code>" is said to be
6975: <dfn export id=concept-element-custom for=Element>custom</dfn>.
6976: 
6977: <p class=note>Whether or not an element is <a for=Element>defined</a> is used to determine the
6978: behavior of the '':defined'' pseudo-class. Whether or not an element is <a for=Element>custom</a> is
6979: used to determine the behavior of the <a href=#mutation-algorithms>mutation algorithms</a>. The
6980: "<code>failed</code>" and "<code>precustomized</code>" states are used to ensure that if a
6981: <a>custom element constructor</a> fails to execute correctly the first time, it is not executed
6982: again by an <a lt="upgrade an element">upgrade</a>.
6983: 
6984: <div class=example id=example-c5b21302>
6985:  <p>The following code illustrates elements in each of these four states:
6986: 
6987:  <pre><code class=lang-html>
6988:   &lt;!DOCTYPE html>
6989:   &lt;script>
